  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9027734d34a03bb43947e2332bd51243, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Dear owner,


    It''s Malai again. I hear the basil pork is doing
    well. Good!


    Pad Thai is the dish every visitor asks me for, so you should
    have it too. When I was young I thought it was too simple to be proud of. Then
    a tourist cried at my table because it reminded her of her honeymoon. Simple
    food carries big memories.


    Soak the noodles, don''t boil them. Shrimp,
    tofu, egg, then the sauce: tamarind, fish sauce, palm sugar. Bean sprouts at
    the very end so they stay crisp.


    Don''t let anyone tell you a small shop
    can''t be a great one.'
